# API Documentation — {{.ProjectTitle}}

## Conventions

- Base path: `/v1` (version prefix on all endpoints)
- Content-Type: `application/json`
- Authentication: Bearer token in `Authorization` header

## HTTP Methods

| Method | Usage |
|---|---|
| `GET` | Read/list resources |
| `POST` | Create a resource |
| `PUT` | Full update of a resource |
| `PATCH` | Partial update of a resource |
| `DELETE` | Delete a resource |

## Standard Response Format

### Success
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "OK",
  "data": { ... }
}
```

### List / Paginated
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "OK",
  "data": [ ... ],
  "meta": {
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "total": 100,
    "total_pages": 10
  }
}
```

### Error
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": [
    { "field": "email", "message": "invalid email format" }
  ]
}
```

## HTTP Status Codes

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 200 | OK — successful GET, PUT, PATCH |
| 201 | Created — successful POST |
| 204 | No Content — successful DELETE |
| 400 | Bad Request — validation error |
| 401 | Unauthorized — missing or invalid token |
| 403 | Forbidden — insufficient permissions |
| 404 | Not Found |
| 409 | Conflict — duplicate resource |
| 422 | Unprocessable Entity — semantic validation failure |
| 429 | Too Many Requests — rate limited |
| 500 | Internal Server Error |

## Authentication

All protected endpoints require:
```
Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
```

Token obtained from `POST /v1/auth/login`.

## Pagination

Query params on list endpoints:
```
?page=1&limit=10
```
Default: `page=1`, `limit=10`, max: `limit=100`.

## Filtering & Sorting

Common pattern:
```
?search=keyword&sort=created_at&order=desc
```

## Rate Limiting

- Default: 100 requests per minute per IP.
- Rate limit headers: `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Reset`.

## Timeout Behavior

- Server-side request timeout: 30s.
- Clients should set their own reasonable timeout.

## API Versioning

Breaking changes are released under a new version prefix (`/v2`).
Non-breaking additions may be added to the current version.
